  "starterCode": "import torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\ndef pytorch_conv2d_from_scratch(x: list, weight: list, bias: list = None) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Conv2d from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\ndef pytorch_conv2d_from_scratch(x: list, weight: list, bias: list = None) -> list:\n    tx, tw = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(weight, dtype=torch.float32)\n    tb = torch.tensor(bias, dtype=torch.float32) if bias is not None else None\n    return torch.round(F.conv2d(tx, tw, bias=tb), decimals=4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
